  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's perception and actuation interface, separating sensor outcomes and motion commands. The specification binds sensor outcomes to safe, coverage-biased actions, enforcing obstacle avoidance, conservative recovery, and rapid return to exploration. Recovery is brief and directed; move_backward is used only for front obstacles, and full_rotate is reserved for deadlock. Exploration alternates between move_forward and random_walk to ensure coverage.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for sensing and motion: one for perception (sensor events), one for actuation (motion commands).",
    "Specification automaton encodes safe, coverage-oriented policy: forward/random_walk in clear, brief directed turns for side obstacles, backward for front obstacle, and rapid return to exploration after recovery."
